      "id": "st-awe-disc-5",
      "title": "Model Sample: 05 · 招有经验的人还是培养新人？· 学术讨论写作范文",
      "professorPrompt": "# 05 · 招有经验的人还是培养新人？· 学术讨论写作范文\n\n> 主题：人力资源管理 ｜ 难度：★★★☆☆ ｜ 目标字数：~155\n\n## 题目\n\n**Professor**: When building a team, is it better to hire experienced workers at higher cost, or to hire young, trainable people at lower cost? What would you advise a new manager?\n\n**Claire (student)**: Always experienced—they hit the ground running and you don't waste time training.\n\n## 范文\n\nI'd push back on Claire a little—I'd advise a *mixed* roster rather than experienced-only.\n\nThe reason is that the two groups cover different needs. Experienced hires, as Claire says, deliver immediately and stabilize tough project",
      "modelResponse": "s. But a good case in point from my lab: when we brought in two junior students and trained them on our signal-processing pipeline, they grew into exactly the roles we needed—at a fraction of the cost, and with deeper loyalty to the team.\n\nAdmittedly, a new manager under deadline pressure should lean experienced to avoid risk. Still, an all-veteran team gets expensive and can resist fresh methods.\n\nUnlike Claire, who defaults to seniority, I'd stress balancing both: seniors for stability, juniors for growth and renewal.\n\n## 中文解析\n\n### 结构拆解\n- 第 1 句：礼貌反驳 Claire，主张\"混合梯队\"。\n- 理由 + 例子：两类人互补；用实验室培养新人的真实经历证明\"低成本+高忠诚\"。\n- 让步：赶工期时确实该偏资深，显务实。\n- 收尾： seniors 稳、juniors 长，呼应同学。\n\n### 亮点表达 / 句型\n- `a *mixed* roster`（混合阵容，HR 类精准词）\n- `hit the ground running`（上任即上手，地道习语）\n- `resist fresh methods`（抵触新方法，点出全资深隐患）\n\n### 写作思路（可借鉴点）\n1. 招聘类题高分答法是\"组合拳\"：不是二选一，而是\"按阶段/风险分配\"。\n2. 用 `A good case in point from my lab` 把例子锚定到自己背景，真实感强、不套路。\n3. 让步句 `Admittedly … Still …` 同时承认对方合理 + 补出盲区，最显成熟度。"
